  "section_notes": "The final rules are strict on incident reporting (24 hours for all incidents, 5 business days for customer notice) and thermal testing (55 °C, 5% limit, no public publication but customer results). They adopt a 12-month new-unit shut-off deadline with a 6-year retrofit plan, 36-month built-in fire suppression, and a mandatory recall at 8/100k with a time-limited regulator-approved remediation plan and prompt customer notices."
